# t9 scenario script: deterministic paragraph replayed by host/t9_scenario_test
# and by the simulator (t9_simulator --script host/scenario_paragraph.t9).
#
# Format, one item per line:
#   <time_ms> press <KEY>
#   <time_ms> release <KEY>
#   <time_ms> expect <text>
#   # comment            (blank lines are ignored too)
# <time_ms> is absolute and non-decreasing. Before each line the replayer calls
# t9_tick(time_ms); press / release call t9_key_press / t9_key_release with it.
# KEY is one of 0-9 NEXT PREV DOT DELETE CANCEL SPELL CAPS MODE ENTER TAB
# FN_ENTER. ENTER is T9_KEY_COMPLETE and TAB T9_KEY_OTHER, with the host's
# Enter / Tab passthrough code. FN_ENTER is the completions toggle (Fn+Enter):
# its press calls t9_set_completions with the opposite setting, its release
# does nothing. Completions start off, as after t9_init. A completion in progress shows as `base[suffix]`.
# expect: after all queued output is applied, the whole host text equals the
# rest of the line after "expect " verbatim. Trailing whitespace would be
# significant, so expectations are placed where the text does not end in one.
# Keys the engine does not handle (t9_key_press returns false) go to the host.
#
# Engine config assumed: multitap_timeout_ms 800, long_press_ms 500, fixture
# dictionary host/t9_fixture_words.txt. Taps are held 40 ms, 150 ms apart;
# SPELL is held 520 ms (a hold starts a spelling in T9); "wait" gaps of
# 1000 ms let a multitap letter time out.

# completions start off (T9_DEFAULT_COMPLETIONS); FN_ENTER turns them on
900 press FN_ENTER
940 release FN_ENTER

